  Maya can run on one GPU, or split the model's layers across several: each then caches the experts of its
  own layers, so together they hold more of them (V100s: ~50 tok/s benchmark on two, ~24 on one).
  1) all 3 together: GPUs 0, 1, 2 (96 GB of VRAM)   (recommended)
  2) GPU 0 (Tesla V100-PCIE-32GB, 32 GB) + GPU 1 (Tesla V100-PCIE-32GB, 32 GB) together
  3) GPU 0 (Tesla V100-PCIE-32GB, 32 GB) only
     (--gpus picks any others, e.g. --gpus 0,2,5; a model with a draft block drafts tokens on two GPUs or more)
